1
00:00:08,973 --> 00:00:13,435
What is it that appears? This
sound. This red. This thought.

2
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:17,057
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

3
00:00:17,137 --> 00:00:21,328
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

4
00:00:22,146 --> 00:00:26,224
Section 1 asked whether one
finished world waits underneath,

5
00:00:26,304 --> 00:00:29,838
seen differently by different
beings. It does not.

6
00:00:29,918 --> 00:00:31,496
What appears is formed.

7
00:00:31,576 --> 00:00:33,864
And nothing is lost in seeing so.

8
00:00:34,678 --> 00:00:39,734
That clears the ground for a quieter
question. Not the world. Not the mountain.

9
00:00:39,814 --> 00:00:44,535
But this sound, this red, this
thought, right now. What is it?

10
00:00:45,349 --> 00:00:48,095
Anatta asks who is behind experience.

11
00:00:48,175 --> 00:00:50,622
Here I ask what the experience itself is.

12
00:00:50,702 --> 00:00:56,288
Most of the big ideas we live by grow out
of how we answer it. Private and public.

13
00:00:56,368 --> 00:01:00,463
Inside and outside. Mind and
matter. Cause and effect.

14
00:01:01,278 --> 00:01:05,437
The usual word for it is
phenomenon. And the word needs care.

15
00:01:05,517 --> 00:01:09,500
In the Middle Way, a phenomenon
is anything that can be known,

16
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:11,429
and every one of them is empty.

17
00:01:11,509 --> 00:01:14,908
But the Abhidharma used the
same word for something else.

18
00:01:14,988 --> 00:01:17,910
A basic element, carrying its own mark.

19
00:01:17,990 --> 00:01:20,764
What is finally there
when the analysis stops.

20
00:01:20,844 --> 00:01:25,261
That second sense is what this section
looks for. And it is never found.

21
00:01:25,341 --> 00:01:29,464
So for what is actually met,
I will just say: what appears.

22
00:01:30,285 --> 00:01:35,069
And I will test the question itself as
I go. What is it? It sounds innocent.

23
00:01:35,149 --> 00:01:37,872
But it may already carry
the given inside it.

24
00:01:38,689 --> 00:01:41,761
As in Section 1, I will not argue first.

25
00:01:41,841 --> 00:01:45,959
I will set two ways of seeing
side by side, three times.

26
00:01:46,039 --> 00:01:47,947
Then we can ask which one holds.

27
00:01:48,803 --> 00:01:50,003
First, a bell.

28
00:01:51,321 --> 00:01:53,102
A temple bell is struck.

29
00:01:53,182 --> 00:01:56,825
The sound is bright,
full, and unmistakable.

30
00:01:56,905 --> 00:02:00,579
Nobody needs to be told it is
there. It fills the courtyard.

31
00:02:01,381 --> 00:02:04,154
Surely, then, the sound is something.

32
00:02:04,234 --> 00:02:07,388
It is vivid, so it must be real in itself,

33
00:02:07,468 --> 00:02:09,154
at least while it rings.

34
00:02:09,234 --> 00:02:12,510
Something has to be there for
the brightness to belong to.

35
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:15,159
And if it is real, it must be somewhere.

36
00:02:15,239 --> 00:02:17,415
Out there in the bell and the air.

37
00:02:17,495 --> 00:02:20,463
Or in here, in my ears and my mind.

38
00:02:21,281 --> 00:02:24,194
Or, and it is a big or, look for it.

39
00:02:25,005 --> 00:02:27,601
Is the sound in the bell? Touch the bell.

40
00:02:27,681 --> 00:02:30,975
There is metal, and a
trembling. Not the sound.

41
00:02:31,777 --> 00:02:34,998
Is it in the air? The air
carries a wave of pressure.

42
00:02:35,078 --> 00:02:37,394
The wave is not the clear tone I hear.

43
00:02:38,213 --> 00:02:42,250
Is it in the ear? The ear has
membranes and small bones.

44
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:43,993
None of them is the sound.

45
00:02:44,793 --> 00:02:48,707
Is it in the mind, then? A little
picture of a bell, kept in here?

46
00:02:48,787 --> 00:02:51,538
Look for that mind. It
is not found either.

47
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:54,247
The sound is not in any of them.

48
00:02:54,327 --> 00:02:56,217
It is not something apart from them.

49
00:02:56,297 --> 00:03:01,557
And it is not their sum, as if bell
plus air plus ear added up to a tone.

50
00:03:01,637 --> 00:03:03,350
Yet it has not gone anywhere.

51
00:03:03,430 --> 00:03:05,162
It is as clear as before.

52
00:03:05,969 --> 00:03:09,448
This is the old test of
Candrakīrti's chariot.

53
00:03:09,528 --> 00:03:11,459
The chariot is not its parts.

54
00:03:11,539 --> 00:03:13,226
Not apart from its parts.

55
00:03:13,306 --> 00:03:15,780
Not their collection, and not their shape.

56
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:18,810
Searched for in every
way, it does not turn up.

57
00:03:18,890 --> 00:03:20,685
Yet it carries its passenger.

58
00:03:20,765 --> 00:03:22,755
The same search works on a sound.

59
00:03:23,565 --> 00:03:25,958
And the sound came only because the bell,

60
00:03:26,038 --> 00:03:30,862
the striking, the air, the ear
and the attention came together.

61
00:03:30,942 --> 00:03:33,516
Take one away, and there is no tone.

62
00:03:34,321 --> 00:03:37,515
So the sound has three
features, all at once.

63
00:03:37,595 --> 00:03:40,966
Vivid: it rings, and it cannot be denied.

64
00:03:41,046 --> 00:03:45,531
Not found: looked for,
it has no core, no edge,

65
00:03:45,611 --> 00:03:47,230
no place where it sits.

66
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:51,501
Dependently arisen: it sounds
only when its conditions meet.

67
00:03:52,338 --> 00:03:55,546
These are not three facts
that happen to coincide.

68
00:03:55,626 --> 00:03:58,526
They are one fact, seen three ways.

69
00:03:59,337 --> 00:04:03,174
And nothing is missing. The bell
still calls the monks to the hall.

70
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:05,891
Second, a red flower.

71
00:04:06,675 --> 00:04:08,511
A red flower by the path.

72
00:04:08,591 --> 00:04:10,712
The red is deep and glowing.

73
00:04:10,792 --> 00:04:14,109
If anything is simply
there, surely a colour is.

74
00:04:14,189 --> 00:04:16,246
No thinking is needed to see it.

75
00:04:17,061 --> 00:04:19,426
Surely the red belongs to the petal.

76
00:04:19,506 --> 00:04:22,809
The petal has it, the way
a box has its contents.

77
00:04:22,889 --> 00:04:25,921
When no one is looking,
the petal is still red.

78
00:04:26,001 --> 00:04:28,996
And seeing only reports
the red that was there.

79
00:04:29,809 --> 00:04:34,203
Or, and again it is a big or,
look at how the red appears.

80
00:04:35,021 --> 00:04:38,460
At noon it glows. At dusk
it goes dark and grey.

81
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:41,354
Under a sodium street lamp it turns brown.

82
00:04:41,434 --> 00:04:46,816
A bee, seeing in ultraviolet, meets a
pattern on the petal that I never see,

83
00:04:46,896 --> 00:04:48,840
and may not meet red at all.

84
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:51,245
For someone with red
green colour blindness,

85
00:04:51,325 --> 00:04:53,410
it is a dull brownish olive.

86
00:04:54,238 --> 00:04:57,433
The red forms with the
light, the petal's surface,

87
00:04:57,513 --> 00:05:02,175
the eye, the kind of body, and
the attention. All in one meeting.

88
00:05:02,255 --> 00:05:06,554
There is no red stored in the petal,
waiting for an eye to fetch it.

89
00:05:07,357 --> 00:05:11,421
Nor is it a private picture in here,
painted by the mind from a colourless

90
00:05:11,501 --> 00:05:16,557
thing out there. That would only move the
stored red from the petal into the head.

91
00:05:16,637 --> 00:05:19,265
And in the head, it is not found either.

92
00:05:20,108 --> 00:05:22,134
Here is the point I most want to make.

93
00:05:22,214 --> 00:05:24,013
It is the easiest to miss.

94
00:05:24,813 --> 00:05:27,939
The red is not first a raw red, and then,

95
00:05:28,019 --> 00:05:29,814
afterwards, dependent.

96
00:05:29,894 --> 00:05:33,007
It does not wait for my
description to become dependent.

97
00:05:33,087 --> 00:05:35,996
It is dependent in the
very moment it is red.

98
00:05:36,076 --> 00:05:40,077
There is no plain layer underneath
that dependence is laid over.

99
00:05:40,897 --> 00:05:45,776
In the same way, the red is singled
out as this red in the seeing itself,

100
00:05:45,856 --> 00:05:50,885
before any word. Designating,
meeting and appearing are one event,

101
00:05:50,965 --> 00:05:52,424
through and through.

102
00:05:53,237 --> 00:05:57,532
And nothing is missing. The red
still guides the bee to the nectar.

103
00:05:57,612 --> 00:05:59,683
And it still stops me on the path.

104
00:06:00,543 --> 00:06:02,519
Third, a passing thought.

105
00:06:03,325 --> 00:06:05,283
Surely a thought is different.

106
00:06:05,363 --> 00:06:10,935
A sound needs air and an ear. But a
thought is mine. Inside. Made of mind.

107
00:06:11,015 --> 00:06:15,677
If anything is real in itself,
it is this thinking, right here.

108
00:06:15,757 --> 00:06:18,630
Doubt everything else,
and still there is this.

109
00:06:19,446 --> 00:06:23,895
Or, and it is the biggest or,
look at a thought as it passes.

110
00:06:24,693 --> 00:06:26,315
I forgot to lock the door.

111
00:06:27,265 --> 00:06:31,261
It arrives vividly. Words.
A faint picture of the door.

112
00:06:31,341 --> 00:06:33,290
A small jolt in the chest.

113
00:06:34,109 --> 00:06:39,015
Where is it? Not in the words. They are
sounds remembered. Not in the picture.

114
00:06:39,095 --> 00:06:41,325
It fades. Not in the jolt.

115
00:06:41,405 --> 00:06:44,604
That is a feeling in the
body. And not apart from them.

116
00:06:45,417 --> 00:06:47,850
And where did it come from? From the door.

117
00:06:47,930 --> 00:06:49,648
From the habit of locking it.

118
00:06:49,737 --> 00:06:54,752
From the hour, the language I learned,
a sound in the street that reminded me.

119
00:06:54,832 --> 00:06:57,909
Take those away, and that
thought does not come.

120
00:06:58,717 --> 00:07:03,623
So the thought is no more a little thing
than the sound is. Vivid. Not found.

121
00:07:03,703 --> 00:07:07,690
Dependently arisen. Exactly
like the bell and the red.

122
00:07:08,489 --> 00:07:13,191
That matters. It closes the way out
that the mind only schools offered.

123
00:07:13,271 --> 00:07:17,797
If the flower is not found out there,
perhaps it is in here, as mind.

124
00:07:17,877 --> 00:07:20,610
Candrakīrti refused that way out.

125
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:24,428
The mind is looked for the same
way, and it is not found either.

126
00:07:24,508 --> 00:07:27,924
Mind and its objects
rise and fall together.

127
00:07:28,725 --> 00:07:32,861
And nothing is missing. The thought
still sends me back to lock the door.

128
00:07:33,673 --> 00:07:38,597
Now, when the search finds nothing,
the mind takes one more quick step.

129
00:07:39,413 --> 00:07:41,099
So the sound is nowhere.

130
00:07:41,179 --> 00:07:45,012
Behind everything there is
a great emptiness. A void.

131
00:07:45,092 --> 00:07:49,228
A silent space, in which
things appear and vanish.

132
00:07:50,062 --> 00:07:54,036
That feels like depth. It is the
easiest mistake to make here.

133
00:07:54,853 --> 00:07:56,648
The absence is not a place.

134
00:07:56,728 --> 00:07:59,664
It is not a background left
over when things are gone.

135
00:07:59,744 --> 00:08:01,960
And it is not a container they appear in.

136
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:07,395
Nāgārjuna warns that those who turn
emptiness into a view are incurable.

137
00:08:07,475 --> 00:08:10,497
Even the word empty is only said to point.

138
00:08:11,310 --> 00:08:16,679
The search removes the assumed thing, and
puts nothing in its place. Not a void.

139
00:08:16,759 --> 00:08:20,420
Not a ground. Not some
reality beyond words.

140
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:25,070
So not found does not mean
nothing. The bell still rings.

141
00:08:25,150 --> 00:08:28,983
It means only this: there was
never a thing there to be found.

142
00:08:29,063 --> 00:08:30,998
And the ringing never needed one.

143
00:08:31,801 --> 00:08:35,049
So, which holds? I test
them as in Section 1.

144
00:08:35,130 --> 00:08:38,926
By experience, by logic,
and by how things work.

145
00:08:39,738 --> 00:08:45,528
By experience. Listen to one sound, now.
Where exactly is it? What is it made of?

146
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:50,827
Could it ring without the ear, the air,
the attention? The sound stays bright.

147
00:08:50,907 --> 00:08:54,332
And nothing is found. No sound
thing behind the hearing.

148
00:08:54,412 --> 00:08:56,234
No hearer behind the sound.

149
00:08:56,314 --> 00:08:58,820
Only hearing, vivid and complete.

150
00:08:59,638 --> 00:09:05,020
By logic. Suppose the sound were real
in itself, with a nature of its own.

151
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:09,327
Then it would depend on nothing. So it
could not arise when the bell is struck,

152
00:09:09,407 --> 00:09:11,596
or stop when the ringing dies.

153
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:14,871
A thing fixed from its
own side could not change.

154
00:09:14,951 --> 00:09:18,132
And what cannot change
cannot appear, or act.

155
00:09:18,212 --> 00:09:22,643
The very vividness the substance
view rests on is the clearest mark of

156
00:09:22,723 --> 00:09:23,923
dependence.

157
00:09:24,674 --> 00:09:27,325
By working. The bell calls the monks.

158
00:09:27,405 --> 00:09:29,119
The red guides the bee.

159
00:09:29,199 --> 00:09:31,225
The thought sends me back to the door.

160
00:09:31,305 --> 00:09:34,621
Each works as a meeting
of conditions, reliably.

161
00:09:34,701 --> 00:09:36,877
And no essence is found doing it.

162
00:09:36,957 --> 00:09:39,014
Function never needed an essence.

163
00:09:39,833 --> 00:09:42,918
So the substance reading
is not the truer view.

164
00:09:42,998 --> 00:09:47,090
It is the default one, carried
by habit and by language.

165
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:51,945
The noun, the sound, quietly sets
up one thing behind the hearing.

166
00:09:52,749 --> 00:09:55,757
What about the question
I began with? What is it?

167
00:09:56,569 --> 00:10:01,774
In everyday life, it is a good question.
What is that sound? The temple bell.

168
00:10:01,854 --> 00:10:06,018
The answer is true. It can be
checked. And it sends me to the hall.

169
00:10:06,834 --> 00:10:10,192
But asked as: what is
it really, in itself?

170
00:10:10,272 --> 00:10:12,733
Then the question already assumes an it.

171
00:10:12,813 --> 00:10:16,089
A thing standing there,
with a nature of its own,

172
00:10:16,169 --> 00:10:18,031
waiting for the right description.

173
00:10:18,111 --> 00:10:21,283
That is the given, slipping
back in through grammar.

174
00:10:22,089 --> 00:10:24,808
Asked that way, the
question has no answer.

175
00:10:24,888 --> 00:10:28,422
Not because the answer is
hidden, or beyond words.

176
00:10:28,502 --> 00:10:32,009
But because there was never an
it, for an answer to be about.

177
00:10:32,089 --> 00:10:35,464
It is like asking where the
fist goes when the hand opens.

178
00:10:36,290 --> 00:10:39,322
The Buddha met questions
like this again and again.

179
00:10:39,402 --> 00:10:41,908
And he did not answer
them on their own terms.

180
00:10:42,713 --> 00:10:46,546
Moḷiya Phagguna asked him:
who feeds on consciousness?

181
00:10:46,626 --> 00:10:49,168
The Buddha said: not a valid question.

182
00:10:49,248 --> 00:10:52,877
The valid question is: for what
is consciousness a condition?

183
00:10:52,957 --> 00:10:55,844
And that he answered,
with dependent arising.

184
00:10:56,661 --> 00:11:02,342
Kassapa asked: is suffering made
by oneself? By another? By both?

185
00:11:02,422 --> 00:11:04,842
By neither, arising by chance?

186
00:11:04,922 --> 00:11:07,708
To each, the answer was: not so.

187
00:11:07,788 --> 00:11:09,873
And then, dependent arising.

188
00:11:10,681 --> 00:11:16,681
Vacchagotta asked where a fire goes
when it goes out. North? South? East?

189
00:11:16,781 --> 00:11:19,853
West? The answer: that does not apply.

190
00:11:19,933 --> 00:11:23,006
The fire burned dependent
on grass and sticks.

191
00:11:23,086 --> 00:11:26,570
When they are used up, there
is no where, for it to go.

192
00:11:27,389 --> 00:11:30,488
Asked, is there a self?
The Buddha was silent.

193
00:11:30,568 --> 00:11:33,355
Asked, is there no self? Silent again.

194
00:11:33,435 --> 00:11:35,828
A yes would side with the eternalists.

195
00:11:35,908 --> 00:11:38,291
A no, with the annihilationists.

196
00:11:39,118 --> 00:11:43,536
To Kaccāna he said: the world
mostly leans on two notions.

197
00:11:43,616 --> 00:11:46,076
It exists, and it does not exist.

198
00:11:46,156 --> 00:11:50,411
Seeing arising and ceasing as
they are, neither takes hold.

199
00:11:50,491 --> 00:11:52,548
The middle is dependent arising.

200
00:11:53,365 --> 00:11:55,921
And he named four ways
of meeting a question.

201
00:11:56,001 --> 00:11:57,578
Some are answered directly.

202
00:11:57,658 --> 00:12:02,746
Some by making distinctions. Some with a
counter question. And some are set aside.

203
00:12:03,545 --> 00:12:06,019
Each time, the move is the same.

204
00:12:06,099 --> 00:12:08,438
The frame of the question is the problem.

205
00:12:08,518 --> 00:12:10,589
So the answer changes the question.

206
00:12:10,691 --> 00:12:16,159
From who, or what is it in itself,
to: dependent on what does it arise?

207
00:12:16,965 --> 00:12:22,487
So vivid, not found, and dependently
arisen is not an answer of the form:

208
00:12:22,603 --> 00:12:25,309
it is X. It names no nature.

209
00:12:25,389 --> 00:12:27,523
It shows how what appears appears.

210
00:12:27,603 --> 00:12:30,938
And why the question of what it
is in itself was never needed.

211
00:12:31,766 --> 00:12:34,716
The question is not
answered. It falls away.

212
00:12:34,796 --> 00:12:39,761
And when it falls away, nothing needs
to fill its place. Not even a void.

213
00:12:40,565 --> 00:12:42,930
And something changes when this is seen.

214
00:12:43,010 --> 00:12:46,857
Each appearance is met as
it is. Vivid, and passing.

215
00:12:46,937 --> 00:12:50,571
With nothing in it to hold,
and no one behind it holding.

216
00:12:51,406 --> 00:12:53,228
That is not a loss of the world.

217
00:12:53,308 --> 00:12:55,692
It is the world, without the weight.

218
00:12:56,509 --> 00:13:00,686
This is Section 2, Part 1 of
the Dependent Arising series.

219
00:13:01,505 --> 00:13:04,862
In Part 2, I follow the
habit when it retreats.

220
00:13:04,942 --> 00:13:08,055
Shown that the sound
does not last, it says:

221
00:13:08,135 --> 00:13:10,637
surely each instant is real.

222
00:13:10,717 --> 00:13:13,680
Shown that the flower
comes apart, it says:

223
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:16,370
surely the smallest pieces are real.

224
00:13:16,450 --> 00:13:19,989
And if the pieces fail,
surely space itself is.

225
00:13:20,818 --> 00:13:25,208
I look for that floor, in
time, in matter and in space.

226
00:13:25,288 --> 00:13:29,642
With Nāgārjuna, Vasubandhu,
and Śāntarakṣita.

